    city: New Plymouth
    country: NZ
    website: "https://mikefentonnz.github.io"
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/MikeFentonNZ/Casio-calculator-datalogger-picaxe-esp-microbit-arduino
url: "https://mikefentonnz.github.io"
abstract: >-
  Timed sensor data logging on Casio FX-9750 and FX-9860 series
  graphing calculators, using undocumented host-wait windows in the
  Casio serial RECEIVE() protocol. A microcontroller holds the
  calculator inside one of those windows while it counts out a
  sampling interval, so the device keeps time and the calculator
  simply receives. No EA-200, no CLAB and no E-CON application are
  required. Supports PICAXE, ESP8266, ESP32 and BBC micro:bit, with
  one calculator program serving every platform.
